module j3.cmp

fn sortBy<T>(xs: []T, less: closure(T, T): bool)
    Sort `xs` so that `less(a, b)` never holds for a later `a` and earlier `b`. Stable: equal elements
    (neither `less`) keep their order, so sorted output is deterministic. Merge sort, O(n log n); the merge
    buffer comes from this thread's scratch arena and is given back before returning (`less` must not keep
    scratch memory it allocates).
